# CANONICAL §7.6 fixture — `AnalyzeEdgeOpRange`, the verb behind "what radius
# will this edge actually take?" (WP4).
#
# WHAT IS PINNED HERE, AND WHAT DELIBERATELY IS NOT.
#
# The measured numbers (`lowerBound`, `bestKnownMax`, `provenUpperBound`,
# `probesUsed`, `searchedRange.max`) are `$any`. They are OCCT's frontier, not a
# protocol fact, and `json_subset` compares numbers EXACTLY — NDJSON is the wrong
# instrument for a value that is allowed to move by less than a nanometre. Their
# pins live in `worker/tests/test_fillet_range.cpp` (9.99925 / 10.0, measured,
# with the derivation), exactly as the OffsetFace pair splits contract from
# corpus.
#
# What IS pinned is everything a Rust or frontend reader parses and BRANCHES on:
# the echo fields, the closure, the classification (`confidence`,
# `monotonicObserved`, `stoppedReason`, `budgetExhausted`, `intervalsTruncated`),
# the authoring floor `searchedRange.min`, and the refusal shape. Those are the
# contract; the millimetres are the measurement.
#
# THE READ-ONLY GUARANTEE is asserted structurally: `GetWorkerHead` is taken
# immediately before and immediately after the analysis and must be IDENTICAL,
# field for field. This verb runs real OCCT builds — dozens of them — and the
# whole reason it may do so from an interactive gesture is that not one of them
# can touch the head. No scratch, no snapshot, no minting, no `bodyEvents`, no
# bin tail.
#
# ARRAY LENGTHS. The harness matcher is a SUBSET match, so listing one entry
# asserts "at least one", not "exactly one". `edges` and `feasibleIntervals` are
# both single-entry here by construction (a box edge has no tangent neighbour,
# and a monotonic frontier yields one run); the exact-count assertions live in
# `test_analyze_edge_op_range.cpp`, which can see the parsed result.
{"expect":{"v":1,"t":"hello","seq":0}}
{"send":{"v":1,"t":"req","id":1,"verb":"OpenSession","args":{"documentId":"doc_analyze_edge_op_range","documentRevision":0,"workerEpoch":4,"mode":"determinism"}}}
{"expect":{"v":1,"t":"resp","id":1,"ok":true,"result":{"sessionOpen":true}}}
